## Code Example

```javascript
// PnP pose estimation sketch (OpenCV.js)
function estimatePose(imagePoints, objectPoints, cameraMatrix, distCoeffs) {
  // SolvePnP returns rotation and translation vectors
  const success = cv.solvePnP(
    objectPoints,    // 3D points in object coordinate system
    imagePoints,     // 2D points in image coordinate system
    cameraMatrix,    // Camera intrinsic parameters
    distCoeffs,      // Distortion coefficients
    rvec,            // Output rotation vector
    tvec             // Output translation vector
  );

  if (success) {
    // Convert rotation vector to rotation matrix
    const R = cv.Rodrigues(rvec);
    return { rotation: R, translation: tvec };
  }
  return null;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests system-level thinking for 3D reconstruction under dynamic scenes and edge-runtime constraints, plus evaluation rigor.

## Key Concepts

- Dense 3D representation (TSDF) with dynamic masking
- Lightweight pose estimation and masked fusion
- Dynamic voxel confidence and decay for occlusions
- Edge latency targets and robust evaluation metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: update TSDF with dynamic masking
function updateVoxelTSDF(voxel, depth, pose, isDynamic) {
  if (isDynamic) return; // skip static updates for dynamic voxels until confirmed
  const sdf = projectDepthToVoxel(depth, pose, voxel.coord);
  voxel.tsdf = (voxel.tsdf * voxel.weight + sdf) / (voxel.weight + 1);
  voxel.weight += 1;
}
```

